# 9. PRAYER CENTRE

This is one of the most important features of the application.

Create a dedicated prayer environment.

It must provide an easy way for people anywhere in the world to submit prayer requests and receive pastoral engagement.

### A. Submit Prayer Request

Create a simple submission form.

Fields:

- Name (optional).
- Email (optional).
- Phone number (optional).
- Prayer category.
- Prayer request description.
- Preferred contact method.
- Privacy preference.

Prayer categories:

- Family and Marriage.
- Health and Healing.
- Career and Employment.
- Financial Needs.
- Spiritual Growth.
- Children and Relationships.
- Thanksgiving.
- Other.

Privacy options:

1. Private: Only authorised assigned pastoral personnel can access it.
2. Prayer Team: Accessible to authorised prayer team members.
3. Public Prayer Wall: Shared with the congregation only after explicit permission and moderation.

Never make private prayer requests public automatically.

### B. Prayer Request Tracking

Allow signed-in users to see their own requests and their status.

Suggested statuses:

- Received.
- Assigned.
- Follow-up.
- Closed.

Provide a simple status history.

Do not expose internal pastoral notes to the person submitting the request.

### C. Pastor Assignment

Authorised administrators must be able to:

- View incoming requests.
- Assign requests to designated pastors.
- Accept responsibility.
- Update status.
- Record follow-up dates.
- Record private pastoral notes.
- Close completed requests.

### D. Prayer Wall

Create an optional moderated community prayer wall.

Members can:

- View approved prayer requests.
- Select "I am praying".
- Send encouragement.

Do not expose private contact information.

### E. Testimonies

Allow members to submit testimonies.

Include:

- Name or anonymous submission.
- Testimony category.
- Description.
- Optional photograph.
- Permission to publish.

All testimonies must be reviewed by an authorised administrator before publication.

